{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560118-a-couple-of-queries-regarding-the-ves","id":1560118,"title":"A couple of queries regarding the VEs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-05-20T04:23:34-07:00","id":1560118,"title":"A couple of queries regarding the VEs","content":"1. It is noticeable that the Void Engineers' Earth Frontier Division doesn't contain any subdivision specialized at desert environment and exploration. Why is it that? It is simply an elision on the part of writers?<br /> <br /> 2. I have previously noted that the Intelligence Directorate of the PDC and Fleet Intelligence Service of R&amp;E share overlapping roles and responsibilities. And it has been alluded the ID assists other Methodologies, particularly the EFD, in surveillance and security operations in the Near Universe. PDC also has its own in-house R&amp;D division, the Void Construction Corps. Why do the VEs as a whole, and PDC in particular, have such a redundant structure?<br /> <br /> 3. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Void Engineers have delved further into the Universe than any other human beings. On the forefront of that effort is the Pan-Dimensional Corps. Its operations take it well past the Spatial Horizon and out into the Deep Universe, establishing beachheads of varying sizes in locales around our galactic volume. Closer to home, the PDC assists the other <i>Conventions</i>, particularly the <i>EFD</i>, in surveillance and security operations in the Near Universe. </div> </div> </div>I think there are some errors in the quoted paragraph. Here, &quot;Conventions&quot; is clearly a misspelling of Methodologies considering the overall context. Do you think the EFD is a misspelling of BCD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-20T06:04:56-07:00","id":1560121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560118-a-couple-of-queries-regarding-the-ves#post1560118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. It is noticeable that the Void Engineers' Earth Frontier Division doesn't contain any subdivision specialized at desert environment and exploration. Why is it that? It is simply an elision on the part of writers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably. All but one were in the original Convention book, so it's really an artifact of the older book's writing.<br /> <br /> That said, if you read down you get:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All of them are comprised of co-ops that determined what was interesting and warranted investigation, without any direct intervention from ETD </div> </div> </div>My takeaway from that is that the organisation is being cast as an organic result of individual member interest as opposed to being centrally co-ordinated. So it's perhaps to be expected that some areas are ignored.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why do the VEs as a whole, and PDC in particular, have such a redundant structure? </div> </div> </div>It's an authoritarian, paranoid, and highly bureaucratic organisation wielding huge military power. Redundancy is to be expected in an organisation where you can't trust other members.<br /> <br /> Frankly, a better question is perhaps why the wider Technocracy isn't like that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you think the EFD is a misspelling of BCD? </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. The next paragraph refers to the EFD having common roots with the PDC, and the EFD have a clear interest in the stuff coming from the near-universe even if it's not their area of expertise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-23T13:21:21-07:00","id":1560166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560118-a-couple-of-queries-regarding-the-ves?p=1560121#post1560121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably. All but one were in the original Convention book, so it's really an artifact of the older book's writing.</div> </div> </div> </div>All but two, if you forgive me being nitpicking; the Revised Convention Book also added the Maintenance and Custodial Division.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, if you read down you get:<br /> <br /> My takeaway from that is that the organisation is being cast as an organic result of individual member interest as opposed to being centrally co-ordinated. So it's perhaps to be expected that some areas are ignored. </div> </div> </div>But the Convention Book explicitly mentions Sahara and Outback deserts as their theatres of operations. The EFD should have a subdivision, or teams, specialized at exploring desert areas on Earth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's an authoritarian, paranoid, and highly bureaucratic organisation wielding huge military power. Redundancy is to be expected in an organisation where you can't trust other members.<br /> <br /> Frankly, a better question is perhaps why the wider Technocracy isn't like that? </div> </div> </div>Fully agree with you on this point. <br /> <br /> If there is one complaint, it is that the introduction of the PDC organization seems lacking in effort compared to other Methodologies. The descriptions of its structural layout and sub-divisions are noticeably brief and cursory in comparison. This is especially true for the ID section; the following is all the information we can get.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With the destruction of the Sentinel network around the Near Horizon and the construction of the ITAG, the Intelligence Directorate (ID) now focuses its energies on monitoring the Deep and Near Universe. It shares that intelligence with the rest of the Convention, frequently clashing with R&amp;E\u2019s FIS. </div> </div> </div>Compared to the much more detailed description of its rival division, FIS, this is quite regrettable.\u200b What do you believe is the root cause of this? Could it be because they'd run out of ideas?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think so. The next paragraph refers to the EFD having common roots with the PDC, and the EFD have a clear interest in the stuff coming from the near-universe even if it's not their area of expertise. </div> </div> </div>A valid point. In this case, I wonder how the Earth-bound EFD could possibility contribute to surveillance and security operation of the wider Convention.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-22T01:07:18-07:00","id":1560851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560118-a-couple-of-queries-regarding-the-ves?p=1560166#post1560166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Convention Book explicitly mentions Sahara and Outback deserts as their theatres of operations. The EFD should have a subdivision, or teams, specialized at exploring desert areas on Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>The EFD should have nothing because this is not their function. They are not the &quot;environment data - gathering for battlefield&quot; division. They are the &quot;explorers going where no human has ever been&quot; people.<br /> <br /> Every Convention is still at its core a collective of Awakened minds that can be Conditioned only so far before they lose the Spark. They are super Scientists, and this is the VE practicing their pure Science.<br /> <br /> Deserts are a known variable. As dangerous as they can get, humanity they're among the environments humanity explored the most, not the least. They're to this day crisscrossed with travel routes and thriving establishments for those weary of the journey.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there must be a Sindicate division dedicated to map all Michelin-worthy restaurants at risk in the desert battlefields. I mean, those not reclaimed by crazed Taftani.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-24T03:20:26-07:00","id":1560930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560118-a-couple-of-queries-regarding-the-ves?p=1560851#post1560851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deserts are a known variable. As dangerous as they can get, humanity they're among the environments humanity explored the most, not the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Posthumanity is presumably referring to this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Inside the safety of the Gauntlet\u2019s cocoon, the Earth Frontier Division (EFD) <b>explores the remaining terrestrial mysteries</b> \u2014 deep ocean trenches, the fields of Antarctica, deep jungles in South America and Asia, parts of the <b>Australian outback</b>, and the <b>Sahara</b>. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}